(BUGS_FOUND #104: `each ... from` over a non-list used to anchor its
 caret at the collection's declaration - the textually first mention of
 its name - rather than at the loop that actually misuses it. `count` is
 declared on line 1 and written on line 2 so the offending `each ... from`
 sits well past both; the caret must land on line 3, not line 1.)

Create a number called count.
Set count to 5.
Print each octet from count.
